Usage: slurm-notify email test --profile <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify email auth refresh --profile <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify email auth status|logout --profile <absolute-path>
       slurm-notify email auth --help
       slurm-notify email --help

Send one experimental synthetic email through SendGrid, Mailgun or Gmail API.
Requires a protected profile and explicit credential references. No scheduler,
state, token refresh or automatic retries during the test.
The separate auth refresh command updates a protected Gmail offline grant;
it never submits email. Foreground API email uses normal enrolled configs; Gmail remains experimental.
Gmail requires an unexpired access token and verified account identity.
API acceptance does not establish inbox delivery or human receipt.
